From: Christian Martinez <xtian437@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_rmnet_rx: unframe accelerated packets on raw-IP transmit

The NSS-to-host node of an rmnet_rx pair hands an accelerated packet back
with an Ethernet header still in front of the IP header: on an AW1000
(IPQ8072, NSS.FW.12.5-210-HK.R) the node's tx byte count exceeds its rx
byte count by exactly 14 per packet, and the frame carries the LAN
client's and the router's addresses with type 0x0800. The bind transmit
callback queued that buffer on the raw-IP device unchanged, so the modem
sent the MAC addresses as the start of the packet. Every LAN flow over
the modem stalled as soon as ECM accelerated it: the TCP and TLS
handshakes pass on the slow path, the first accelerated upstream
segment never reaches the peer.

Strip the frame in the callback, which only the firmware calls, and set
the protocol from the IP version field, as the receive side does.

Tested with qmi_wwan_q (Quectel RG500Q-EA, QMAP, raw IP): LAN downloads
and uploads over the modem accelerate and complete.
---
--- a/nss_rmnet_rx.c	2026-10-03 00:51:45.855758981 +0800
+++ b/nss_rmnet_rx.c	2026-10-03 00:51:57.973741995 +0800
@@ -824,9 +824,36 @@
 /*
  * nss_rmnet_rx_bind_xmit()
  *	Transmit an accelerated packet on the raw-IP device.
+ *
+ * The firmware hands the packet over still framed with the Ethernet header
+ * of the flow's other side, which a raw-IP device would send as part of the
+ * packet. Only the firmware calls this, so the frame is always there.
  */
 static void nss_rmnet_rx_bind_xmit(struct net_device *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
+	if (unlikely(skb->len < ETH_HLEN + sizeof(struct iphdr))) {
+		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	skb_pull(skb, ETH_HLEN);
+
+	switch (skb->data[0] & 0xf0) {
+	case 0x40:
+		skb->protocol = htons(ETH_P_IP);
+		break;
+
+	case 0x60:
+		skb->protocol = htons(ETH_P_IPV6);
+		break;
+
+	default:
+		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	skb_reset_mac_header(skb);
+	skb_reset_network_header(skb);
 	skb->dev = dev;
 	dev_queue_xmit(skb);
 }
